      "id": "claim_23cb0bc159594e839a3b762b96cc1bae",
      "statement": "The package-source policy forbids Snap entirely (D-021) and restricts the Ubuntu archive to the NVIDIA driver, build toolchains, and library headers only; applications must come from PyPI, a GitHub release, a direct binary, or Hugging Face. The toolchain-not-application distinction is annotated in-block (build-essential, python3-venv, pkg-config, libreadline-dev, zlib1g-dev, libicu-dev, libssl-dev, libpcre2-dev, zstd), while each application is built from upstream source or installed from its language package index.",
