    {
      "id": "claim_2dab27c2b2334ae1980ac83d87c7f2f3",
      "statement": "The PostgreSQL block builds from the official postgresql.org source tarball (owner decision: source build, not PGDG): it verifies the tarball against HX_POSTGRES_SHA256 (exit 30 on mismatch), runs ./configure --prefix=/srv/postgresql --with-openssl --with-icu, make, make install, initdb, sets listen_addresses='*' and confirms it is active, appends a pg_hba scram-sha-256 rule for HX_LAN_CIDR guarded against matching a commented line, and uses a Type=notify unit. It prints the instruction to set the postgres password out-of-band and never in the repo.",
      "evidence": [
